# Documentation workflow

- Inspect existing files before writing. Do not overwrite correct completed work without cause.
- Write one chapter at a time at full textbook depth. Prefer one finished chapter over many shallow drafts.
- Never create empty chapter placeholders or empty module assessments marked complete.
- Status values: `Not started`, `In progress`, `Drafted`, `Needs review`, `Needs revision`, `Completed`.
- Mark `Completed` only after the depth gate and review checklist in `DOCUMENTATION-STANDARDS.md` pass.
- Follow `.cursor/skills/java-documentation/SKILL.md`.
- Attribute a subagent review only if that agent was actually invoked or its review was genuinely performed.
- After a full module's chapters are `Completed`, create its assessment under `assessments/module-assessments/` with solutions in a separate file.
- Update `PROGRESS.md` only to match reality.
- Target Java **21**. Verify version-sensitive claims against official docs. Record real `javac`/`java` results.
